+# MASTER7 v154 supplier catalogue boundary safety release
+
+Release: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.154-provider-boundary-safety`
+
+This release hardens the read-only catalogue boundary for EVO888H5, CLOTPLAY,
+Pragmatic Play and Venus Gaming.
+
+- EVO validates the response envelope, game IDs, names, duplicates and maximum
+  size, hides raw provider bodies and keeps unknown title availability closed.
+- CLOTPLAY validates pagination, row fields, duplicates, maximum size and exact
+  page completeness. Missing maintenance stays closed.
+- Pragmatic Play no longer treats catalogue presence as proof that a title is
+  available.
+- Venus Gaming titles remain maintenance and unapproved remote thumbnails are
+  withheld.
+- The Portal keeps EVO titles suspended and preserves the last complete
+  snapshot when a malformed refresh is received.
+
+The suppliers remain blocked externally: EVO code 130, Pragmatic HTTP 435,
+CLOTPLAY HTTP 403 and missing Venus response-signature headers. These conditions
+cannot be bypassed safely and no Play action is exposed.
+
+No player, launch, balance, wallet, transfer, settlement, recovery or payment
+operation is enabled by this release. VPay, GSPAY, 1MPay, payment switches,
+credentials, service plans and DNS are unchanged.
